There seems to be a small hole at the base of one of the boulders.	其中一顆巨石底部似乎有個小洞。
An extremely large jumble of boulders sits in the center of this heavily wooded area.  At the base of one, you see a small hole.	這片茂密樹林的中央堆著一大堆巨石。你看見其中一顆的底部有個小洞。
You notice a small hole at the base of one of the craggy boulders in the center of the clearing.	你注意到，空地中央嶙峋巨石的底部有個小洞。
It seems to have a green tinge to it, but it's so faint you can't tell for sure.	它似乎帶著一抹綠色，但太過微弱，讓你無法確定。
What glow?	什麼光芒？
The ancient, mossy rock has seen many winters.  There is a small hole at its base.	這塊佈滿青苔的古老岩石，已經歷過許多個寒冬。它的底部有個小洞。
From where you're standing, it appears to be nothing more than a large rock.	從你站的地方看去，它似乎只是一塊大石頭。
Congratulations!  You now have all three of Daventry's lost treasures!  Now don't waste any time; bring the treasures straight back to King Edward before it's too late.	恭喜！你已經找齊了戴凡確王國失落的三件寶物！別再浪費時間了，趁一切還來得及，趕緊把寶物帶回去給愛德華國王。
You'll have to move closer.	你得靠近一點才行。
Large moss-covered trees surround a shallow, swampy lake.	長滿青苔的大樹，環繞著一座淺淺的沼澤湖。
Spotting the snake in the treetops you wisely decide that there are better trees to climb than this one.	你發現樹梢上有條蛇，明智地決定去爬別棵樹。
You'll wind up with a useless dead snake and a guilty conscience.	到頭來你只會得到一條沒用的死蛇，還有滿滿的罪惡感。
The snake's small red tongue flicks at the air, tasting your presence in the swamp.	蛇的小紅舌頭在空氣中吐信，感應著你在沼澤裡的存在。
Even if the snake could hear you, it wouldn't have anything to say.	就算蛇聽得懂你說話，牠也無話可說。
The huge snake is watching you very closely, and its intentions are less than friendly.	那條巨蛇正緊盯著你，來意顯然不太友善。
Numerous flowers are growing in the fertile soil.	肥沃的土壤裡開滿了各式花朵。
The flowers' fragrance is enticing.	花朵散發出誘人的香氣。
It would be a shame to pick the lovely wildflowers.	摘下這些美麗的野花實在太可惜了。
Lovely wildflowers grow profusely in this beautiful green meadow.	這片美麗的綠色草原上，遍地盛開著可愛的野花。
A mighty beanstalk has sprouted from the magic beans you planted!  Around the beanstalk, several varieties of wildflowers are growing.	你種下的魔豆長出了一株雄偉的豆莖！豆莖四周開著好幾種野花。
The wildflowers are very beautiful here.	這裡的野花非常美麗。
A natural rock bridge crosses the steep, slippery banks of the river here.	這裡有一座天然的石橋，橫跨過又陡又滑的河岸。
As the troll pushes you back your ring slips off your finger and into the raging river below. It's lost forever!	矮精靈把你推了回去，戒指從你的手指上滑落，掉進下方湍急的河水中。它永遠消失了！
The water is particularly perilous as it passes downstream through this gully.	河水流經這道溝壑往下游而去時，格外危險。
GNOME: "How in the world did you think of that?  That's not even close."	矮人：「你到底是怎麼想到那個的？差得可遠了。」
You weren't invited into the gnome's house.	矮人並沒有邀請你進去他家。
There's a rock over by the bush, but this rock is nothing compared to the one the gnome lives in!	灌木叢旁有塊石頭，但跟矮人住的那塊比起來根本不算什麼！
The gnome's house is carved right into the rock between three trees.	矮人的家就鑿在三棵樹之間的岩石裡。
The broad leaves provide shade for the gnome during the hot summer months.	寬大的樹葉在炎熱的夏季為矮人遮蔭。
The roots of the three trees grow freely around the gnome's house.	三棵樹的樹根，恣意地在矮人家周圍蔓生。
This hole, carved into the side of the rock, is the entrance to the gnome's home.  It's too dark inside to make out any details, and the gnome probably prefers it that way.	這個鑿在岩壁上的洞口，就是矮人家的入口。裡頭太暗了，看不清任何細節，矮人大概也樂得如此。
The wizened gnome went inside his house.	那位乾瘦的矮人走進了他家裡。
You see a wizened old gnome sitting in front of his house, whittling.	你看見一位乾瘦的老矮人，坐在家門前削著木頭。
You are speaking with a wizened old gnome.	你正在和一位乾瘦的老矮人說話。
You see a wizened old gnome walking to his house.	你看見一位乾瘦的老矮人正走回家去。
Why?  The gnome has done nothing to you.	為什麼？矮人又沒對你做過什麼。
The gnome isn't here.	矮人不在這裡。
You won't need any straw on your quest.	你的冒險用不到稻草。
The gnome spun that gold out of straw! You can't take it, but don't worry. If you needed it, the gnome would give it to you.	矮人把那些黃金用稻草紡出來的！你不能拿走，不過別擔心，如果你需要，矮人自然會給你。
The spinning wheel helps the gnome make his living. Please don't take it.	這台紡車是矮人賴以維生的工具，請別拿走它。
Only gnomes know how to do that.	只有矮人才懂得怎麼做那件事。
Now what in the world would you do with a gnome?	你到底要拿一個矮人來做什麼？
GNOME: "Ooooh, very close, very close!  But not quite right!"	矮人：「噢～很接近了，很接近了！但還不完全對！」
The gnome is busy whittling, and doesn't notice you.	矮人正忙著削木頭，沒注意到你。
What do you think I am, a car?  This also won't get you a raise.  Nice try.	你以為我是什麼，一輛車嗎？這樣也加不了薪。想得美。
GNOME: "Please, keep guessing, won't you?"	矮人：「拜託，繼續猜嘛，好不好？」
GNOME: "Really, Sir Graham!"	矮人：「格拉漢爵士，真是的！」
The gnome momentarily pauses in response to the mysterious voice, then resumes his whittling.	矮人聽到這個神秘的聲音，停頓了一下，接著又繼續削木頭。
GNOME: "You still haven't guessed my name!"	矮人：「你還沒猜出我的名字呢！」
The gnome can't hear you from there!	你站在那裡，矮人聽不見你說話！
GNOME: "Where did you get that idea?  That's not even close!"	矮人：「你這想法是打哪來的？差得可遠了！」
GNOME: "You have only one guess left, Sir Graham!"	矮人：「格拉漢爵士，你只剩最後一次機會了！」
The gnome momentarily pauses in response to the mysterious voice, then resumes his whittling	矮人聽到這個神秘的聲音，停頓了一下，接著又繼續削木頭
The gnome is busy whittling, and doesn't hear your guess.  Move closer and give it another try.	矮人正忙著削木頭，沒聽見你的答案。靠近一點，再試一次吧。
GNOME: "That's right!  Outstanding!  I didn't think you were THAT clever."	矮人：「答對了！太厲害了！沒想到你有這麼聰明。」
GNOME: "As a reward for your sharp intellect, here are some beans.  They're no ordinary beans, but it's up to you to find out why."	矮人：「為了獎勵你的機智，這裡有一些豆子。它們可不是普通的豆子，至於為什麼，就由你自己去發現吧。」
GNOME: "Somebody as smart as yourself should have no problem at all.  <giggle>"	矮人：「像你這麼聰明的人，這應該難不倒你才對。〈竊笑〉」
GNOME: "Well, step over here so I can give them to you."	矮人：「來，走過來這邊，讓我把它們交給你。」
GNOME: "You didn't guess my name, but I am still going to help you, Sir Graham."	矮人：「格拉漢爵士，雖然你沒猜中我的名字，但我還是會幫你的。」
GNOME: "Take this golden key.  It will aid you on your quest, Sir Graham, but it's up to you to find out how!"	矮人：「格拉漢爵士，拿去這把金鑰匙。它會在你的冒險中幫上忙，至於怎麼用，就由你自己去發現吧！」
GNOME: "Well, step over here so I can give it to you."	矮人：「來，走過來這邊，讓我把它交給你。」
GNOME: "Here you are.  Good luck on your quest."	矮人：「拿去吧。祝你冒險順利。」
GNOME: "Er, pardon me, Sir Graham, but you're blocking my home.  I have other adventurers to help and other puzzles to pose!"	矮人：「呃，格拉漢爵士，不好意思，你擋住我家的門了。我還有其他冒險者要幫忙、還有其他謎題要出呢！」
GNOME: "Thank you, Sir Graham."	矮人：「謝謝你，格拉漢爵士。」
GNOME: "So, you've come back!  Good for you, Sir Graham!"	矮人：「哦，你又回來了！格拉漢爵士，真有你的！」
GNOME: "Welcome, Sir Graham.  I have been expecting you."	矮人：「歡迎，格拉漢爵士。我一直在等你。」
GNOME: "I have something that will be of great use to you.  But first, Sir Graham, you must answer this riddle.  I'll give you three guesses.  What is my name?"	矮人：「我有樣東西對你會很有用。不過格拉漢爵士，你得先回答這個謎題。我給你三次機會，猜猜我叫什麼名字？」
GNOME: "It's been delightful chatting with you, Sir Graham.   I get so few visitors... Perhaps it's the fault of that thickheaded troll."	矮人：「格拉漢爵士，跟你聊天真愉快。我這裡訪客實在不多……也許都要怪那個榆木腦袋的矮精靈。」
mad	生氣
really mad	非常生氣
It is of no use to keep guessing the gnome's name.	再繼續猜矮人的名字也沒有用了。
GNOME: "You have only one guess left."	矮人：「你只剩最後一次機會了。」
GNOME: "You still have two guesses."	矮人：「你還有兩次機會。」
This is the gnome's spinning wheel.	這是矮人的紡車。
This is a pile of gold.	這是一堆黃金。
There is a small pile of straw here.	這裡有一小堆稻草。
As the troll pushes you back your ring slips off and falls into the river, to be lost forever.	矮精靈把你推了回去，戒指滑落，掉進河裡，永遠消失了。
The river ripples as it rushes over the rocks.	河水沖過岩石，激起陣陣漣漪。
You can just walk out of the river.	你可以直接走出河流。
The swift current is making it impossible to swim.	湍急的水流讓你根本無法游泳。
Off to one side is a clear blue lake surrounded by a pretty meadow.  A swift river flows into the lake.	一旁是一座清澈的藍色湖泊，四周環繞著美麗的草原，一條湍急的河流注入湖中。
The pretty meadow surrounds the clear blue lake.	美麗的草原環繞著這座清澈的藍色湖泊。
The clear blue lake is surrounded by a pretty meadow.	這座清澈的藍色湖泊，四周環繞著美麗的草原。
The river gets to be rather rough around these parts.	河水流到這一帶變得相當湍急。
You glance under the old bridge, but see nothing unusual.	你瞄了一眼舊橋底下，沒發現什麼異常。
There are some large rocks jutting out of the river here.	這裡的河面上突出幾塊大石頭。
There are rocks and small boulders all along the lakeshore.	湖岸邊到處是石頭和小巨石。
You see a clear blue lake surrounded by a pretty meadow.	你看見一座清澈的藍色湖泊，四周環繞著美麗的草原。
The pretty meadow surrounds a clear blue lake.	美麗的草原環繞著一座清澈的藍色湖泊。
The river, barely visible off to the west, empties into the lake.	西邊隱約可見的河流，注入了這座湖泊。
A few trees sit near a clear blue lake.	幾棵樹佇立在一座清澈的藍色湖泊旁。
This is a jumping fish.  You'd jump, too, if you lived in such cold water!	這是一條會跳躍的魚。要是你也住在這麼冷的水裡，也會跳個不停！
At the moment, you'd only be able to see the fish from underwater!	此刻，你只有潛到水裡才看得見這條魚！
The fish would do you no good except to attract the attention of every cat in the kingdom!	這條魚對你一點用也沒有，頂多只會引來全王國貓咪的注意！
In the condition the cottage is in, that might be dangerous.	以這間小屋目前的狀況來看，這麼做恐怕很危險。
Upon closer inspection you realize this poor cabin doesn't even have a door.	你仔細一看才發現，這間破舊的小屋根本連門都沒有。
The roof is sadly in need of reshingling. It leaks in several dozen places.	這屋頂實在需要重新鋪瓦了，好幾十個地方都在漏水。
This is the saddest-looking roof you've ever seen.  Made of thatched bark, it clearly won't keep the rain out.  It's sagging slightly, too...it looks like it might fall in if it isn't repaired soon!	這是你見過最悽慘的屋頂了。它是用茅草樹皮蓋成的，顯然擋不住雨水，而且還有點下陷……看起來要是再不修，很快就會塌下來！
The chimney seems to be the only part of the cottage that doesn't need repairing.	這間小屋似乎只有煙囪不需要整修。
Inside, you can see the woodcutter feeding stew to his wife.  Somehow, the shaky little hut looks cheerier inside already!	你看見屋裡的樵夫正餵妻子喝燉肉湯。不知怎地，這間搖搖欲墜的小屋，裡頭看起來已經開朗多了！
When you look in the doorway, you see a poor starving woodcutter and his wife.	你朝門口望去，看見一位可憐挨餓的樵夫和他的妻子。
From where you're standing, you can see that the cottage doesn't even have a door.	從你站的地方看去，你發現這間小屋根本連門都沒有。
It was made from rough, hand-hewn logs long ago.  Lately, the upkeep has faltered.  There are even holes in the roof.	這是很久以前用粗糙的手削原木蓋成的。近來乏人維護，屋頂上甚至還有破洞。
Through the small paneless window, you see a very relieved woodcutter feeding hot stew to his wife.	透過那扇沒有玻璃的小窗，你看見一位如釋重負的樵夫，正餵妻子喝熱騰騰的燉肉湯。
Through the small paneless window, you see a poor starving woodcutter and his bedridden wife.	透過那扇沒有玻璃的小窗，你看見一位可憐挨餓的樵夫和他臥病在床的妻子。
You are unable to see in the window from here.	你在這裡沒辦法看進窗戶裡。
You're standing too far away from the house to see inside.	你離這間房子太遠了，看不見裡面。
There is a window on the front of the house.	房子正面有一扇窗戶。
You see the cottage of the poor woodcutter and his wife.  You helped them both tremendously by giving them the magic bowl of hot stew.	你看見這間可憐樵夫夫妻倆住的小屋。你送給他們那個裝滿熱燉肉的魔法碗，幫了他們很大的忙。
You see a cottage in shambles.  It saddens you to think that somebody might still live there.	你看見一間破敗不堪的小屋。一想到可能還有人住在裡面，你就感到難過。
Perhaps you should go inside the cottage for a better look.	也許你該進去小屋裡看個仔細。
You can't see inside the door from where you're standing.  Perhaps if you moved a little closer.	你站在這裡看不進門內，也許再靠近一點會比較好。
An old axe is permanently wedged into the tree stump.	一把老斧頭牢牢卡在樹樁裡，怎麼也拔不出來。
The handle has been broken and repaired.  The head shows the signs of many sharpenings.	斧柄斷過又修補過，斧頭上滿是多次磨利的痕跡。
The trees were cut from these stumps years ago with this ax.	多年前，這些樹樁上的樹木就是用這把斧頭砍下的。
The trees were cut from these stumps years ago.	多年前，這些樹木就是從這些樹樁上砍下的。
The old axe is tightly wedged in the tree stump.  You cannot remove it no matter what you do.	這把老斧頭緊緊卡在樹樁裡，不管你怎麼做都拔不出來。
How are you going to use the axe when you can't even get it out of the stump?	你連斧頭都拔不出樹樁，要怎麼用它？
It is an ancient, rusty water pump.  It probably doesn't even work.	這是一台老舊生鏽的手壓幫浦，恐怕根本不能用了。
The rusty pump doesn't work.	這台生鏽的幫浦壞了。
You need to get closer.	你得靠近一點。
You need to go inside to do that.	你得先進到裡面才能這麼做。
You can't do that now.	你現在還不能這麼做。
There isn't a glass pane in this window.	這扇窗上沒有玻璃。
You are not close enough.	你離得不夠近。
You should really try to find the door.	你真的該想辦法找到門才對。
You see the back of the old tumbledown cottage, badly in need of repair.	你看見這間搖搖欲墜的老舊小屋的背面，急需整修。
A patchwork of old boards keeps the house together.	幾塊拼湊起來的舊木板，勉強撐住這間房子。
Perhaps you should go inside the house for a better look.	也許你該進去房子裡看個仔細。
You could get a much better view if you were a little bit closer.	你要是再靠近一點，視野會清楚許多。
